Rem ==================================================================
Rem spiro-keys.shoddy — the spirograph, under your hands.
Rem
Rem Run: mill run spiro-keys.shoddy   (or open it and press Ctrl+R)
Rem      Up / Down change the turn angle by a degree and redraw.
Rem      Q or Escape closes the window.
Rem
Rem spiro.shoddy draws once and returns. This one keeps a loop going:
Rem it asks the window for the next event, does something about it, and
Rem calls itself again. That recursion IS the loop — there is no while,
Rem and nothing changes in place; the angle travels as an argument and
Rem every redraw hands back a new turtle.
Rem
Rem NextEvent BLOCKS until something happens, so a program waiting on a
Rem keypress uses no processor at all. Programs that animate ask for a
Rem tick instead (SetFps) — that is what the mills in mills/ do.
Rem
Rem Every branch below calls Loop directly, which makes it a genuine
Rem tail call: the weave turns it into a jump, so this can run all day
Rem without the stack growing.
Rem ==================================================================

Include "turtle.shoddy"
Include "scribbler.shoddy"
Include "keys.shoddy"
Include "spiro-core.shoddy"

Rem One step of the plan, drawn — the same words as spiro.shoddy.
Def Draw(t As Turtle, s As Step) As Turtle
    Let inked = SetPenColor(t, Red(s), Green(s), Blue(s))
    TurnRight(Forward(inked, Ahead(s)), Turn(s))

Rem Angles that still make a pattern: 90 exactly closes the square and
Rem draws nothing new, and the extremes wander off the window.
Def AngleIn(a As Number) As Number
    Max(60, Min(120, a))

Rem Wipe the surface, send the turtle home, draw the whole plan again at
Rem this angle, and say which angle it is in the title bar. Home keeps
Rem the pen and colour and resets only position and heading, so every
Rem redraw starts exactly as the first draw did.
Def Redraw(t As Turtle, angle As Number) As Turtle
    Let cleared = ScribblerFill(Sc(t), 0, 0, 0)
    Let home = Home(t)
    Let drawn = Fold(PlanWith(defaultSteps, angle), home, Draw)
    Let named = Title(drawn, "Shoddy Spirograph - angle " & Str(angle) & " - Up/Down, Q quits")
    Blit(named)

Def Loop(t As Turtle, angle As Number) As Turtle
    Select Case NextEvent(Sc(t))
        Case ScribblerKeyDown(key, mods, at)
            Select Case ClassifyKey(key)
                Case ArrowUp
                    Let up = AngleIn(angle + 1)
                    Loop(Redraw(t, up), up)
                Case ArrowDown
                    Let down = AngleIn(angle - 1)
                    Loop(Redraw(t, down), down)
                Case EscKey
                    Close(t)
                Case CharKey(c) Where c = Asc("Q")
                    Close(t)
                Case Else
                    Loop(t, angle)
        Case ScribblerQuit
            Close(t)
        Case Else
            Loop(t, angle)

Def Main()
    Let start = NewTurtle(640, 480)
    Let shown = Redraw(start, turnAngle)
    Let done = Loop(shown, turnAngle)
    Print("closed")
